@@ -16,4 +16,7 @@ identify a value in the document.
 
 Applies an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) to a JSON document and
 returns a new document without mutating the input. Supports `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`,
-`copy`, and `test`; invalid patches and failed operations throw an error.
+`copy`, and `test`; invalid patches and failed operations throw an error. Both arguments must be
+JSON values (so, for example, sparse arrays and `undefined` are rejected), including operation
+members that RFC 6902 otherwise ignores. Patch validation and application use detached working
+copies, so a failure leaves both supplied arguments unchanged.
